*******************===============**************

Part2  add github actions - every time main branch code commit to remote repo- trigger the build and auto deploy
*******************===============**************
1. Prepare your Vite config

Update vite.config.ts:

import { defineConfig } from 'vite'
import react from '@vitejs/plugin-react'

export default defineConfig({
  plugins: [react()],
  base: '/your-repository-name/',
})

Replace your-repository-name with your GitHub repo name.

Example:

base: '/my-react-app/'


2. Enable GitHub Pages

Go to your repository:

Settings
 → Pages
 → Build and deployment

Set:

Source: GitHub Actions  *****

3. Create GitHub Actions workflow

Inside your project create:

.github/
 └── workflows/
      └── deploy.yml

Add this file:
deploy.yml:
-----------
name: Deploy React App to GitHub Pages

on:
  push:
    branches:
      - main

permissions:
  contents: read
  pages: write
  id-token: write

jobs:
  build:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest

    steps:
      - name: Checkout
        uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - name: Setup Node
        uses: actions/setup-node@v4
        with:
          node-version: 20
          cache: npm

      - name: Install dependencies
        run: npm install

      - name: Build project
        run: npm run build

      - name: Upload build files
        uses: actions/upload-pages-artifact@v3
        with:
          path: ./dist

  deploy:
    needs: build
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest

    environment:
      name: github-pages
      url: ${{ steps.deployment.outputs.page_url }}

    steps:
      - name: Deploy to GitHub Pages
        id: deployment
        uses: actions/deploy-pages@v4
		
		
4. Commit and push
git add .
git commit -m "Add GitHub Pages deployment"
git push origin main

5. Check deployment

Go to:

GitHub Repository
 → Actions

You will see:

Deploy React App to GitHub Pages

When it finishes successfully, your site will be available at:

https://username.github.io/repository-name/


6. Future updates

After this setup, every time you run:

git add .
git commit -m "Update app"
git push

GitHub Actions will automatically:

Install dependencies
Run Vite build
Deploy the new dist folder
Update GitHub Pages

No need to run npm run deploy anymore.